From 049d2995af3bb0232b7299e88339fc0d93f23528 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:40:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Lab: XCL_SPARSE_SCATTER=1 on the fix-waits tree
 (ad96e43b from S/wwts)

Cherry-picked from ad96e43b (port of S/wbench 39dcd1e6 + 45fbf328 +
0945e7a9, scatter only): with the switch, upload_dirty sends a sparse
slot's changed runs to the windows by one compute dispatch
(sparse_scatter.hlsl, compiled at run time like indirect_clamp, built
off the submitting threads) instead of one CopyBufferRegion a run.
Off unless XCL_SPARSE_SCATTER=1.

Two conflicts in sparse.rs resolved by hand against the call stats
wrapping of 31fab203: State::signal keeps cs!(QueueSignal, ..) and
adds FENCE_SIGNALLED.store; upload_dirty's copy branch keeps
cs!(RecCopyBuffer, ..) and adds UPLOAD_CMDS[0]. The scatter writes go
on the sparse queue before its signal, so XCL_SPARSE_MAP_NOWAIT's Map
copy (ordered after that signal) and XCL_FENCE_DIRECT=2's landings see
them as they see the copies. No file in TRANSLATOR_SOURCES.

(cherry picked from commit ad96e43b)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
